    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "199310d9_2121256a",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T18:53:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you need to lock this mutex befor the `is_owner_dev()` check. If not, I think the possible scenario could lead to a race condition (using UAF as an example):\n\nAfter dropping the spin lock, a separate thread from the driver uses the same `dev` pointer that owns the buffer, and invokes `wrapfd_put_mappable()`, which opens the door for another thread to close() the wrapfd and release it freeing the associated data structures. Then, when we come back to this thread, we\u0027ll use memory that\u0027s been freed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1525,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1528,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "f4889840fb9175df41b2de6d9ac20502f6912c34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e234d039_a8c7100a",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T19:19:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would be a bad user design because `wrapfd_add_listener()` is supposed to be called only when the driver owns the buffer and if there is a race with `wrapfd_put_mappable()` then you can\u0027t guarantee that the driver owns it (if `wrapfd_put_mappable()` wins the race).\n\nI don\u0027t think we can lock `listeners_lock` before `is_owner_dev()` because that would introduce dependency between `ctx-\u003elock` and `listeners_lock` which can lead to a deadlock. I\u0027ll think more about ways we can handle this in a better way but I think this race should be prevented from the user side (making sure `wrapfd_add_listener()` is not racing with `wrapfd_put_mappable()`).",
      "parentUuid": "199310d9_2121256a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1525,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1528,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "f4889840fb9175df41b2de6d9ac20502f6912c34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9115629f_a007eebc",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T20:33:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which scenario would result in a deadlock between `ctx-\u003elock` and `listeners_lock`?",
      "parentUuid": "e234d039_a8c7100a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1525,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1528,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "f4889840fb9175df41b2de6d9ac20502f6912c34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b24f0c8_e57f3065",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T20:40:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`wrapfd_del_listener()` takes `ctx-\u003elock` and then `listeners_lock`. If I restructure this function to do the same then we will avoid a possible deadlock. I\u0027ll try that and post an update if everything pans out as I expect it to.",
      "parentUuid": "9115629f_a007eebc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1525,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1528,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "f4889840fb9175df41b2de6d9ac20502f6912c34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6be78114_44461594",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T21:23:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But `wrapfd_del_listener()` cannot take `listeners_lock` after `ctx-\u003elock` because after `ctx-\u003elock` is taken, the thread is in atomic context; you\u0027d need to take the locks in the other order each time, and if you do that every time you need to take both locks, then I do not think you\u0027ll have a deadlock?",
      "parentUuid": "3b24f0c8_e57f3065",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1525,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1528,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "f4889840fb9175df41b2de6d9ac20502f6912c34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
